@districts
title: Address the districts
subtitle: dev: kf_right_dissent −5, workers_kpd +2×m
unavailable-subtitle: [? if head_timer > 0 : [+ head_timer +] months before the chairman can act again. ?]
choose-if: head_timer = 0
on-arrival: head_timer = 3; kf_right_dissent -= 5; workers_kpd += 2*campaign_mult

Brandler travels the districts, from Chemnitz to the Ruhr, and speaks to the functionaries as one who has stood at a bench himself. The Right takes heart, Pieck's apparatus is reassured, and the workers hear a chairman who talks about wages.

@zentrale
title: Chair the Zentrale on the united front
subtitle: dev: y23_unity +1, kf_left_dissent +3, trust +2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if head_timer > 0 : [+ head_timer +] months before the chairman can act again. ?]
choose-if: head_timer = 0
on-arrival: head_timer = 3; y23_unity += 1; kf_left_dissent += 3; comintern_trust += 2

A long session of the Zentrale ends in a resolution for joint action with the SPD locals and the unions. Moscow reads it with approval, and the Left reads it as one more concession to the leaders who put down the revolution.

@executive
title: Report to the Executive
subtitle: dev: trust +6, kf_left_dissent +2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if head_timer > 0 : [+ head_timer +] months before the chairman can act again. ?]
choose-if: head_timer = 0
on-arrival: head_timer = 3; comintern_trust += 6; kf_left_dissent += 2

Brandler reports to the Executive of the Comintern. He is polite and prepared, and he is noted down as a loyal man who argues his case. The Left, who think the Comintern should be obeyed rather than argued with, find the argument excessive.

@governments
title: Press for workers' governments
subtitle: dev: kf_right_strength +4, kf_left_dissent +3, y23_unity +1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if head_timer > 0 : [+ head_timer +] months before the chairman can act again. ?]
choose-if: head_timer = 0
on-arrival: head_timer = 3; kf_right_strength += 4; kf_left_dissent += 3; y23_unity += 1

Brandler argues that workers' governments in the Saxon and Thuringian states would put police and administration at the party's disposal, and bring SPD workers with us. The Left says it ties the party to the very leaders it should be exposing.
